[ti:PyTorch Media Processing: Three Libraries, Clearer Roles]
[ar:Ava & Brian]
[al:PyTorch Blog Podcast]
[00:00.00]Ava: You want to train a model on video, but first you've got to choose a decoder.
[00:00.00]Ava：想用视频训练模型，首先得选个解码器。
[00:04.71]Why does that feel like a research project before the research project?
[00:04.71]怎么感觉研究还没开始，就得先做一番研究？
[00:09.40]Brian: That's exactly the problem this article addresses.
[00:09.40]Brian：这正是这篇文章要解决的问题。
[00:12.84]PyTorch has brought media decoding and encoding together in TorchCodec.
[00:12.84]PyTorch 通过 TorchCodec 统一了媒体解码和编码。
[00:17.73]There's now a clearer answer to where your images, video, and audio should enter the system.
[00:17.73]现在，图像、视频和音频该从哪里进入系统，有了更明确的答案。
[00:24.41]Ava: And I'm guessing this matters even more when the model generates media.
[00:24.41]Ava：我猜模型生成媒体内容时，这一点更重要。
[00:28.89]You need a way to get the result back out, too.
[00:28.89]还得有办法把结果输出出来。
[00:32.20]Brian: Right.
[00:32.20]Brian：没错。
[00:32.67]Decoding turns media files or encoded bytes into tensors, the arrays a model works with.
[00:32.67]解码把媒体文件或编码后的字节转换成张量，也就是模型处理的数组。
[00:39.55]Encoding takes tensors back into media files.
[00:39.55]编码则把张量转换回媒体文件。
[00:43.07]Generative models need that return journey.
[00:43.07]生成式模型也需要这一步。
[00:46.78]Ava: Let's get the names straight.
[00:46.78]Ava：先把几个名字理清楚。
[00:48.93]I'm Ava, a software engineer outside the PyTorch core team.
[00:48.93]我是 Ava，一名不在 PyTorch 核心团队的软件工程师。
[00:53.30]Brian, you're here to help me understand who does what.
[00:53.30]Brian，你来帮我弄清楚各个库负责什么。
[00:57.72]Brian: Gladly. TorchCodec handles decoding and encoding.
[00:57.72]Brian：好啊。TorchCodec 负责解码和编码。
[01:01.67]TorchVision transforms images and video. TorchAudio transforms audio.
[01:01.67]TorchVision 负责图像和视频变换，TorchAudio 负责音频变换。
[01:07.22]Think of TorchCodec as the entrance and exit, with transforms doing work on tensors in between.
[01:07.22]可以把 TorchCodec 看作入口和出口，变换操作则在中间处理张量。
[01:15.23]Ava: When you say transforms, you mean operations that change the data, like cropping an image?
[01:15.23]Ava：你说的变换，是指裁剪图像这类改变数据的操作？
[01:21.75]Brian: Exactly. We'll get to a crop example shortly.
[01:21.75]Brian：对。稍后我们会讲一个裁剪的例子。
[01:25.03]The basic division is straightforward: move between media and tensors with TorchCodec, then use the other two libraries to transform those tensors.
[01:25.03]分工很简单：用 TorchCodec 在媒体和张量之间转换，再用另外两个库变换张量。
[01:36.11]Ava: Okay, take me back. What made the old setup confusing?
[01:36.11]Ava：好，先说说以前的情况。旧方案为什么让人困惑？
[01:40.33]Having a vision library and an audio library sounds reasonable.
[01:40.33]一个视觉库、一个音频库，听起来挺合理。
[01:45.61]Brian: The difficulty was that decoding and encoding were scattered and partly duplicated.
[01:45.61]Brian：问题是解码和编码功能分散在各处，还有部分重复。
[01:51.39]Each library built its own stack.
[01:51.39]每个库都建立了自己的一套处理方式。
[01:53.69]Even within TorchVision, video reading had multiple entry points and three backends, meaning different underlying implementations.
[01:53.69]即使在 TorchVision 内部，读取视频也有多个入口和三种后端，也就是三种底层实现。
[02:03.09]Ava: Three backends for video?
[02:03.09]Ava：视频有三种后端？
[02:04.72]That already sounds like a choice I'd rather make after coffee. What were the options?
[02:04.72]光听着就觉得得先喝杯咖啡再选。都有哪些？
[02:10.67]Brian: There was PyAV in Python, a C plus plus backend using FFmpeg, a media processing library, and a CUDA backend for NVIDIA graphics processors.
[02:10.67]Brian：有 Python 版的 PyAV、使用媒体处理库 FFmpeg 的 C++ 后端，以及用于 NVIDIA 图形处理器的 CUDA 后端。
[02:22.64]Only the PyAV option was available out of the box.
[02:22.64]只有 PyAV 开箱即用。
[02:27.26]Ava: Wait, so choosing another backend also meant taking on build work?
[02:27.26]Ava：等等，选其他后端还得自己编译？
[02:32.63]Brian: Yes.
[02:32.63]Brian：对。
[02:32.92]The other two required building from source, and they were tied to a specific FFmpeg version.
[02:32.92]另外两种都需要从源码构建，而且依赖特定版本的 FFmpeg。
[02:39.66]TorchAudio also had readers and writers for video and audio, plus additional audio decoding utilities with different backends.
[02:39.66]TorchAudio 也提供视频和音频的读取与写入功能，另有采用不同后端的音频解码工具。
[02:49.13]Ava: And image decoding lived in TorchVision.
[02:49.13]Ava：图像解码则在 TorchVision 里。
[02:52.13]I can see how the answer to 'where do I decode this? ' could get complicated.
[02:52.13]难怪“我该在哪里解码？”会变成复杂的问题。
[02:58.27]Brian: That's the background. Over the last two years, the team consolidated the media stack.
[02:58.27]Brian：背景就是这样。过去两年，团队整合了媒体处理功能。
[03:04.84]TorchCodec now brings together decoding and encoding for images, video, and audio, on CPUs, or central processing units, and CUDA.
[03:04.84]现在 TorchCodec 统一提供图像、视频和音频的解码与编码，支持 CPU（中央处理器）和 CUDA。
[03:15.13]Ava: The article gives three reasons for that move, right?
[03:15.13]Ava：文章给出了这样调整的三个理由，对吧？
[03:18.59]Let's start with the one users feel directly.
[03:18.59]先说用户最有感受的那个。
[03:21.89]Brian: One place to go. Media I/O, meaning input and output, now belongs in TorchCodec.
[03:21.89]Brian：入口统一了。媒体 I/O，也就是输入和输出，现在都由 TorchCodec 负责。
[03:28.06]Users get a library designed as a whole, instead of having to choose among separate interfaces spread across libraries.
[03:28.06]用户可以使用一套统一设计的库，不必在分散于各个库的接口之间做选择。
[03:37.60]Ava: So there's less detective work before I can start. What's the second reason?
[03:37.60]Ava：这样开始之前就不用费劲摸索了。第二个理由呢？
[03:42.99]Brian: Performance work has a clear home.
[03:42.99]Brian：性能优化有了明确的落脚点。
[03:45.46]Previously, effort was spread across implementations, and it wasn't obvious which one should receive an optimization.
[03:45.46]以前，精力分散在不同实现上，也不清楚该优化哪一个。
[03:53.99]Now improvements go into TorchCodec, where users can share the benefit.
[03:53.99]现在改进都集中在 TorchCodec，用户也能共同受益。
[03:59.51]Ava: Does the article say it's actually faster, or just easier to optimize?
[03:59.51]Ava：文章说它确实更快，还是只说更容易优化？
[04:05.26]Brian: It says TorchCodec is generally more performant than the previous implementations, particularly for CUDA video decoding.
[04:05.26]Brian：文章说 TorchCodec 通常比之前的实现性能更好，尤其是在 CUDA 视频解码方面。
[04:13.60]But it doesn't give benchmark numbers or test conditions.
[04:13.60]但文章没有提供基准测试数据或测试条件。
[04:17.56]We can't turn that into a specific speedup.
[04:17.56]所以不能据此给出具体的加速倍数。
[04:20.90]Ava: Fair enough. What's the third reason?
[04:20.90]Ava：有道理。第三个理由呢？
[04:23.81]I suspect someone had a very long list of dependencies.
[04:23.81]我猜有人列了一长串依赖项。
[04:28.47]Brian: They did.
[04:28.47]Brian：确实如此。
[04:29.15]At the time of writing, the stack involved six major FFmpeg versions, four through nine.
[04:29.15]写作本文时，这套技术栈涉及 FFmpeg 4 到 9，共六个主要版本。
[04:35.77]It also involved NVIDIA's codec development kit for decoding on a GPU, or graphics processing unit.
[04:35.77]还需要 NVIDIA 的编解码器开发套件，用 GPU（图形处理器）解码。
[04:43.56]Ava: And images bring their own libraries into the picture?
[04:43.56]Ava：处理图像也得引入专门的库吧？
[04:47.37]Brian: Yes, libraries such as libjpeg and libpng for different image formats.
[04:47.37]Brian：对，比如处理不同图像格式的 libjpeg 和 libpng。
[04:52.48]These dependencies also have licensing rules affecting what can ship.
[04:52.48]这些依赖项还有许可要求，会影响哪些内容可以随软件发布。
[04:57.53]And they're C or C plus plus libraries, rather than pure Python dependencies.
[04:57.53]而且它们是 C 或 C++ 库，并非纯 Python 依赖。
[05:03.51]Ava: Which makes builds and releases harder. The complexity hasn't disappeared, then.
[05:03.51]Ava：这就让构建和发布更难了。所以复杂性并没有消失。
[05:09.35]It's been gathered into one place.
[05:09.35]只是被集中到了一处。
[05:12.19]Brian: Exactly. That place is TorchCodec.
[05:12.19]Brian：没错，这一处就是 TorchCodec。
[05:14.84]It greatly reduces the maintenance burden for TorchVision and TorchAudio.
[05:14.84]它大大减轻了 TorchVision 和 TorchAudio 的维护负担。
[05:20.53]To recap this part: users get one entry point, optimization gets one home, and dependency maintenance gets contained.
[05:20.53]总结一下：用户有了统一入口，优化有了统一归处，依赖维护也集中起来了。
[05:30.01]Ava: Let's move on to those other libraries. They used to offer much more than transforms.
[05:30.01]Ava：再说说另外两个库。它们以前提供的远不止变换功能。
[05:35.95]What's happening to models and datasets?
[05:35.95]模型和数据集现在怎么样了？
[05:39.09]Brian: TorchVision and TorchAudio are now focused on transforms.
[05:39.09]Brian：TorchVision 和 TorchAudio 现在专注于变换功能。
[05:43.27]The rest of their broad feature set isn't under active development.
[05:43.27]它们原先提供的其他大量功能已不再积极开发。
[05:48.19]The article points to the wider ecosystem, including HuggingFace libraries, for models, datasets, and pipelines.
[05:48.19]文章建议通过更广泛的生态系统，包括 HuggingFace 的库，来获取模型、数据集和流水线。
[05:56.75]Ava: Why draw the boundary there? Is that based on how people use the libraries?
[05:56.75]Ava：为什么把边界划在这里？是根据大家的使用情况决定的吗？
[06:02.26]Brian: Yes. The team observed that transforms were the most active usage areas.
[06:02.26]Brian：对。团队观察到，变换功能是使用最活跃的部分。
[06:07.46]Models, datasets, and pipelines had lagged as alternatives grew.
[06:07.46]随着替代方案发展，模型、数据集和流水线方面的功能逐渐落后。
[06:12.08]Narrowing the scope lets the team concentrate on strengths that other ecosystem tools don't cover.
[06:12.08]缩小范围后，团队就能专注于其他生态工具没有覆盖的优势领域。
[06:19.50]Ava: That sounds sensible, but changing the boundaries of a library can hurt existing users.
[06:19.50]Ava：听起来合理，但调整库的功能范围可能影响现有用户。
[06:25.82]How rough was this transition?
[06:25.82]这次过渡有多不顺利？
[06:28.35]Brian: The article says it was particularly disruptive for TorchAudio.
[06:28.35]Brian：文章说，对 TorchAudio 用户的影响尤其大。
[06:33.15]Many APIs, meaning application programming interfaces, were deprecated and eventually removed.
[06:33.15]许多 API（应用程序编程接口）先被标记为弃用，最终被移除。
[06:40.32]Community feedback also changed the plan: several popular APIs originally marked for removal were kept.
[06:40.32]社区反馈也改变了计划：一些原定移除的热门 API 被保留了下来。
[06:48.52]Ava: That's a useful detail.
[06:48.52]Ava：这点很值得一提。
[06:50.25]We shouldn't hear 'smaller library' and assume every older feature vanished.
[06:50.25]不能一听说“库变小了”，就以为所有旧功能都没了。
[06:56.29]Brian: Right. The article doesn't list those retained APIs here.
[06:56.29]Brian：对。文章这里没有列出具体保留了哪些 API。
[07:00.32]Its argument is that a smaller TorchAudio can actually be maintained, giving users something they can continue to rely on.
[07:00.32]文章的观点是，规模更小的 TorchAudio 才能得到持续维护，让用户继续放心使用。
[07:09.31]Ava: Let's make this concrete. Suppose I've got a video file.
[07:09.31]Ava：说具体点吧。假设我有一个视频文件。
[07:13.45]Walk me through the example without making me listen to every bracket.
[07:13.45]带我过一遍这个例子，别逐个念那些括号。
[07:18.97]Brian: Deal. TorchCodec's VideoDecoder opens the file.
[07:18.97]Brian：好。TorchCodec 的 VideoDecoder 会打开文件。
[07:22.64]The example selects ten frames, starting at frame index ten and stopping before twenty.
[07:22.64]示例从索引为 10 的帧开始，取到索引 20 之前，共十帧。
[07:29.43]That returns a FrameBatch, a batch object containing the frame data.
[07:29.43]它返回一个 FrameBatch，也就是包含帧数据的批量对象。
[07:35.09]Ava: What does that frame data look like before the transforms touch it?
[07:35.09]Ava：变换处理之前，帧数据是什么样的？
[07:39.62]Brian: It's a tensor of unsigned eight-bit values.
[07:39.62]Brian：它是一个由无符号 8 位数值组成的张量。
[07:42.86]Its dimensions are frames, channels, height, and width.
[07:42.86]它的维度依次是帧、通道、高度和宽度。
[07:47.01]The example passes that data into TorchVision's v2 transforms, meaning its version two transform interface.
[07:47.01]示例把这些数据传给 TorchVision 的 v2 变换，也就是第二版变换接口。
[07:55.42]Ava: And that's where the crop happens?
[07:55.42]Ava：裁剪就是在这一步做的？
[07:58.03]Brian: Yes.
[07:58.03]Brian：对。
[07:58.32]It combines RandomResizedCrop, a random crop and resize operation with an output size of two hundred twenty-four, and ToDtype.
[07:58.32]它组合了 RandomResizedCrop 和 ToDtype；前者随机裁剪并缩放，输出尺寸为 224。
[08:07.56]The latter converts the data to thirty-two-bit floating point, with scaling enabled.
[08:07.56]后者将数据转换为 32 位浮点数，并启用数值缩放。
[08:14.08]Ava: So the handoff is the tensor.
[08:14.08]Ava：所以传递给变换的是张量。
[08:16.19]The decoder gets the frames out, and the transforms prepare those frames for what comes next.
[08:16.19]解码器提取帧，变换则为后续处理准备这些帧。
[08:23.33]Brian: Exactly. Audio follows the same pattern.
[08:23.33]Brian：没错。音频也是同样的流程。
[08:26.30]TorchCodec's AudioDecoder reads all the samples in the example.
[08:26.30]示例中，TorchCodec 的 AudioDecoder 会读取全部采样数据。
[08:30.98]Those samples go into TorchAudio's MelSpectrogram transform, which represents audio in terms of time and frequency using the mel scale.
[08:30.98]这些采样数据传给 TorchAudio 的 MelSpectrogram 变换，用梅尔刻度表示音频随时间变化的频率信息。
[08:41.34]Ava: There's also a sample rate in that example. Where does it come from?
[08:41.34]Ava：那个示例里还有采样率。它是从哪里来的？
[08:46.37]Brian: From the decoded samples. The example uses that sample rate to configure MelSpectrogram.
[08:46.37]Brian：来自解码后的样本。示例用这些样本的采样率来配置 MelSpectrogram。
[08:52.74]Images follow the same overall pattern: decoding returns plain tensors that can go straight into TorchVision's version two transforms.
[08:52.74]图像也遵循同样的模式：解码得到普通张量，可以直接传给 TorchVision 的 v2 变换。
[09:02.78]Ava: And when the model produces something we want to save, we head back through TorchCodec?
[09:02.78]Ava：模型生成了想保存的内容时，就再交给 TorchCodec？
[09:08.67]Brian: Yes.
[09:08.67]Brian：对。
[09:09.00]The article names VideoEncoder, AudioEncoder, JpegEncoder, and PngEncoder for that direction.
[09:09.00]文章提到，这一步可用 VideoEncoder、AudioEncoder、JpegEncoder 和 PngEncoder。
[09:16.70]The key point is the same across media: decode, transform the tensors, and encode when you need a media file.
[09:16.70]各种媒体的关键步骤都一样：解码、变换张量，需要媒体文件时再编码。
[09:26.06]Ava: There's one more change for framework engineers: releases.
[09:26.06]Ava：对框架工程师来说，还有一个变化：发布方式。
[09:30.55]What does ABI stable mean here?
[09:30.55]这里说的 ABI 稳定是什么意思？
[09:33.30]Brian: ABI means application binary interface.
[09:33.30]Brian：ABI 指应用程序二进制接口。
[09:36.32]The article says all three libraries are now ABI stable.
[09:36.32]文章说，这三个库现在都实现了 ABI 稳定。
[09:40.65]A given library version isn't tied to just one PyTorch version; it keeps working with subsequent PyTorch versions.
[09:40.65]某个库版本不再只对应一个 PyTorch 版本，后续的 PyTorch 版本也能继续使用它。
[09:49.83]Ava: So they don't need a rebuild for every PyTorch release?
[09:49.83]Ava：所以每次 PyTorch 发布新版本，都不用重新构建这些库？
[09:53.90]Brian: Correct. Their release schedules no longer match PyTorch's, and that's expected.
[09:53.90]Brian：没错。它们的发布周期不再与 PyTorch 同步，这是预期之内的。
[09:59.70]For users still decoding or encoding through TorchVision or TorchAudio, the article recommends moving to TorchCodec, starting with the migration guide.
[09:59.70]仍通过 TorchVision 或 TorchAudio 解码、编码的用户，文章建议从迁移指南入手，转用 TorchCodec。
[10:11.00]Ava: And if something's missing?
[10:11.00]Ava：如果缺少某项功能呢？
[10:13.22]Brian: Report it on GitHub.
[10:13.22]Brian：到 GitHub 上反馈。
[10:14.55]There's also a follow-up post planned about new features and getting the most performance from a full decoding and transform pipeline.
[10:14.55]后续还计划发一篇文章，介绍新功能，以及如何让完整的解码与变换流程发挥最佳性能。
[10:23.42]This article establishes the direction, but leaves those details for later.
[10:23.42]本文明确了方向，具体细节留待后续介绍。
[10:28.74]Ava: Let's finish with three things to remember.
[10:28.74]Ava：最后总结三点。
[10:32.23]First, use TorchCodec for decoding and encoding images, video, and audio.
[10:32.23]第一，用 TorchCodec 解码和编码图像、视频及音频。
[10:38.50]Brian: Second, use TorchVision for image and video transforms, and TorchAudio for audio transforms.
[10:38.50]Brian：第二，用 TorchVision 处理图像和视频变换，用 TorchAudio 处理音频变换。
[10:45.48]Look to the wider ecosystem for the other needs discussed here.
[10:45.48]本文提到的其他需求，可以在更广泛的生态中寻找解决方案。
[10:50.61]Ava: Third, the smaller scopes and ABI stability change maintenance and releases.
[10:50.61]Ava：第三，职责范围缩小和 ABI 稳定会改变维护与发布方式。
[10:55.95]Expect independent release schedules, and plan your move from the older media interfaces.
[10:55.95]各库会独立发布，也要规划好从旧媒体接口迁移。
[11:02.55]Brian: Thanks for listening, and we'll catch you next time.
[11:02.55]Brian：感谢收听，我们下次再见。
